From 6c0ee265362b5cd22786f38f21806465c064b502 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: osy <osy@turing.llc>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 01:02:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] ui/spice: carry the guest scanout's pixel format to the
 IOSurface

The shared IOSurface was created with a hardcoded 'BGRA' pixel format,
and that format was hardcoded again at every consumer, including the
fourcc reported to the client through spice_qxl_gl_scanout().

A scanout is in whatever format the guest allocated. That is normally
BGRA, but a fullscreen D3D swapchain becomes the scanout directly and may
be R8G8B8A8, so its bytes ended up in a surface every consumer read as
BGRA and red and blue came out transposed. Windowed output was unaffected
because the scanout is then the desktop primary, which is BGRA.

Take the format from the scanout MTLTexture, recreate the surface when it
changes just as for a size change, and report the real fourcc.
SpiceGlScanout.format is documented as the drm fourcc format; it was
being filled with a constant.

The EGL path takes the format too. The CGL path cannot: for 8-bit colour
CGLTexImageIOSurface2D only accepts GL_BGRA with
GL_UNSIGNED_INT_8_8_8_8_REV, and that combination reads the surface as
BGRA no matter what its fourcc says, so a non-BGRA surface there is
refused rather than silently transposed. Only the Metal path is ever
asked for a different order.

